\code{band = "mad"}, use \verb{trend + seasonal +/- k * 1.4826 * MAD(remainder)},
the MAD computed on the weeks used in the fit of that pass.

\strong{Passes.} Pass 1 smooths the series as observed and flags the observed
weeks outside the band (\code{flag_1}). Pass 2 sets the flagged weeks to \code{NA}
(with \code{flag_na = "isolated"}, only the weeks of \code{isolated} runs) and
smooths again, re-choosing \code{K} and the smoothing parameters; the flags
are recomputed on all observed weeks against the pass-2 fit (\code{flag_2}),
so a week can be unflagged. If the set of weeks to exclude changes, a
further pass is run with the new set, up to \code{max_iter} re-smoothings
(pass \code{max_iter + 1}). When the set of flags of pass 1 is empty, pass 1
is final. \code{flag} holds the flags against the final fit (consistent with
\code{band_lo}, \code{band_hi}) and \code{excluded} the weeks set to missing in the
final fit; they coincide when the procedure converged (column
\code{converged} of \code{fits}).

\strong{Flag types} (per run of consecutive flagged weeks of \code{flag}):
\code{final} when the run touches the last 4 weeks of the series; otherwise
\code{isolated} when it is shorter than \code{run_min} weeks; otherwise
\code{level_shift} when the median of the 8 unflagged observed weeks after
the run minus the median of the 8 before it (on the seasonally adjusted
scale, \code{observed - seasonal}) is at least the median band half-width
over the run in absolute value, and \code{interruption} when it is smaller or
cannot be computed (run at the start of the series).

\strong{Cost.} Each pass chooses \code{K} with \code{(max_harmonics + 1) * (n_backfit + 1)} fits of the smooth Kalman model, then fits the method
(\code{n_backfit + 1} trend fits; \code{gam_ar1}: one \code{bam} per value of \code{rho}).
